  "root_adjudication": [
    "Reset generation strictly increases from an actual non-null prior; checked workspace revision remains distinct and does not imply +1 generation arithmetic.",
    "The authenticated original request/result/transition receipt must resolve exact scope, full context, controller, FileSafe, permission and capability. Read-only resolver views introduce no Browser physical record or runtime proof.",
    "A committed reset followed by failed/unknown event append is recovery-required with a known effect. Only the original append identity may reconcile; retry does not reset again, claim no effect or rewind a newer generation.",
    "The sole historical Browser consumer reads verified reset boundaries without live generation/controller authority, a separate durable projection, UsageRecord, prompt delivery or artifact dereference.",
    "The exact new filtered checkpoint adopts complete SP-278 root/generation/anchor/frontier/source/read-snapshot joins. Complete examined global range differs from the last matching reset. Source/permission/deletion fences and exact prior-value CAS gate advance and disclosure.",
    "Same-key current plus at most two closed retired cores make retention physical. Stable generation identity/birth/history, actual first withdrawal, exact predecessor transaction, full hold/ref resolution, capacity reservation and eligible-only cleanup preserve the existing policy. Native transaction/hold observations remain assumptions in the synthetic model.",
    "Only reset is added in this landing. All existing registry rows and retention policies are unchanged. The other Browser admissions remain individually pending."
  ],
